  "document": "Édouard Roger-Vasselin\nÉdouard Roger-Vasselin (] ; born 28 November 1983) is a male tennis player from France. He won the men's doubles title at Roland Garros in 2014, partnering Julien Benneteau. He is the son of 1983 French Open semifinalist Christophe Roger-Vasselin."
